==English==

===Etymology===
* From {{etyl|la|en}} {{m|la|prōverbiālis}}; {{suffix|proverb|ial|lang=en}}

===Pronunciation===
* {{a|UK}} {{IPA|/pɹəˈvɜɹb.iː.əl/|lang=en}}

===Adjective===
{{en-adj}}

# Of, resembling, or expressed as a [[proverb]], [[cliché]], [[fable]], or [[fairy tale]].
#* '''1947''', ''[[w:Miracle on 34th Street|Miracle on 34th Street]]'' ([http://www.script-o-rama.com/movie_scripts/m/miracle-on-34th-street-script.html transcript]):
#*: Doris: You're making me feel like the '''proverbial''' stepmother.
# Widely [[known]]; [[famous]]; [[stereotypical]].
#: ''I grew up in a prefab house on Main Street in 1950s suburbia, the second and last child of a '''proverbial''' nuclear family.''

